--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -65,6 +65,23 @@ The included `Dockerfile` and `Procfile` use the same WSGI entrypoint. Persist
 the `instance/` database and `static/uploads/` storage, or replace them with
 managed database/object storage before a multi-instance deployment.
 
+## Deploying on Vercel
+
+Vercel's filesystem is read-only, so SQLite and local uploads don't work there.
+
+1. In the Vercel project: Storage / Marketplace -> add a Postgres database (e.g. Neon) and connect it to the project. This sets `DATABASE_URL`.
+2. Project Settings -> Environment Variables: add `SECRET_KEY` (long random string). Optionally `PAYSTACK_*`, `SMTP_*`, `TWILIO_*`.
+3. From your own machine, once, create roles/categories and the first admin:
+
+       set DATABASE_URL=<the same Postgres URL>
+       set ADMIN_EMAIL=you@example.com
+       set ADMIN_PASSWORD=<12+ chars>
+       python init_db.py
+
+4. Redeploy. Static files live in `public/static/` (Vercel serves `public/` from its CDN).
+
+Known limitation: image uploads (avatars, style/service photos) are written to `/tmp` and do not persist on Vercel. Use the image URL fields, or add object storage (Vercel Blob / Cloudinary).
+
 ## Tests
 
    python -m pytest -q
